640	      /* After A/B operand evaluation:
641	       *
642	       * addrA holds the A-pointer, which is always a read-pointer.
643	       * AA_Value holds the A field of the A-operand (NEW_MODES & RWLIMIT).
644	       * IR.A_value holds the B field of the A-operand.
645	       *
646	       * addrB holds the B-write-pointer.
